    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8cc232d8_757ca3f5",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/nct38xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-14T17:00:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this should set both CC lines to the designated pull regardless of polarity. DUTs present Rd or Rp resistors on both CC lines always.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 143,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 143,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "73b4f825506d6bbd86bce4abeaa3ffe32d90d0b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9018dab9_629a3383",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/nct38xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160634
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-17T12:12:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem is that the existing code is not fully compatible with TCPC spec, and therefore we had to override it with this function.\nPlease refer to the TCPC spec  Revision 2.0, Version 1.0, Figure 4-16 (TCPC State Diagram after a Connection)\nYou will see under the Attached.Src  state the following text “Drive one CC line based on RC Do not drive CC line that has VCONN connected”.\nSo the pull value (Rd or Rp) should be applied only to one CC line (according to the connection polarity) and the other CC line should stay Open.\nSetting both CC lines to the same value will result in a wrong CC status and wrong connection handling.",
      "parentUuid": "8cc232d8_757ca3f5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 143,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 143,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "73b4f825506d6bbd86bce4abeaa3ffe32d90d0b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "16ee52ea_816dd1b2",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/nct38xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-22T16:37:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That is one scenario that we only need to apply a single CC resistor. When we are connecting as a SNK should we apply Rd on both CC lines.\n\nBasically, this is only every applying a single CC resistor, are there not any cases in the spec were we need to apply resistor to both CC lines?\n\nIt seems that we should clean up common code, to follow the spec better to specify when only a since CC line should be updated and the update all drivers at that point.\n\n\n----\n\n\nAlso, how poorly does this driver behave if you don\u0027t have this special logic? It seems like we shouldn\u0027t add the special logic here, but make this behave like common code expects then change the common code to follow the spec better.",
      "parentUuid": "9018dab9_629a3383",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 143,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 143,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "73b4f825506d6bbd86bce4abeaa3ffe32d90d0b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "37a2807a_589ba4a0",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/nct38xx.c",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1160634
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-02-24T10:05:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Applying a resistor to both CC lines should happens only when there is no connection (when calling tcpci_tcpc_drp_toggle() ). Once there is a connection one CC line is used for communication and the other is used for Vconn (and therefore should be left Open).\nAnyhow I agree that the correct fix is to change the common code and then we will be able to fix and simplify this function.",
      "parentUuid": "16ee52ea_816dd1b2",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 143,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 143,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "73b4f825506d6bbd86bce4abeaa3ffe32d90d0b8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
